  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Supporting MS to address hydrological challenges, extremes and water scarcity</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The activity will strengthen international scientific cooperation to address unsolved problems in hydrology, cryosphere, hydrological extremes (flood and drought), sediment and erosion transport and water scarcity and challenges in Member states and their efforts to meet the targets set under the Sendai Framework for DRR, and SDGs. IHP will promote scientific research to enhance understanding of water availability from the cryosphere and call for science-based policy decisions. IHP-IX will strengthen the adaptation capacity of countries to climate change impacts through assessment, promotion of regional cooperation, and stakeholder engagement.

The activity will contribute to Priority Area 1 Scientific research and innovation and to Priority Area 4: IWRM under conditions of global change.</narrative>
  </description>
